# Effect (JS/TS)

Effect is how JS/TS does async work, errors, and validation.

- ALWAYS `Effect.gen` / `Effect.tryPromise` / `Data.TaggedError` / `Match` for
  async work, failures, and tagged unions.
- A server cache (Query or the project’s equivalent) stays a cache. `run*`
  functions are the only edge runners that call `Effect.runPromise`.
- NEVER `new Promise`. NEVER export `async` from `api/` or `domain/` except
  `run*` edge runners. NEVER raw `fetch` outside one `api-client` module.
  NEVER `throw` in `api/` or `domain/`.
- NEVER Zod, neverthrow, or hand-rolled boundary validation. Use `effect/Schema`
  (`100-strong-types`).
